                                                "sense_id": "72932ea4-fa40-3c02-b096-9725b2258193",
                                                "text": "Ralph Walker, a white small landowner, remembered farmers swapping chickens or hogs for wheat in the 1930s. Many others described similar barterings of vegetables, fish, wild berries, fruit, and labor among members of extended families […]"
